<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yelü Dashi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1087">1087</a>–<a href="/years/1143">1143</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Emperor Dezong of Western Liao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yelü Dashi was a Khitan prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty</a> who fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> in its final years. When the Jurchen Jin destroyed the Liao in 1125 he led followers west into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balasagun">Balasagun</a> and proclaimed himself Gurkhan, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-khitai">Qara Khitai</a>. In 1141 he defeated the Seljuk sultan Sanjar at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qatwan">Battle of Qatwan</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The prince <b>Yelü Dashi</b> had already led a band of followers west in 1124, and in Central Asia he founded the Qara Khitai, or Western Liao, which lasted until 1218.</blockquote><a href="/empire/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1122 two groups of Khitans fled west; one was led by <b>Yelü Dashi</b>, who joined the Liao emperor Tianzuo on the Western Xia border.</blockquote><a href="/empire/qara-khitai">Qara Khitai · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Qocho became a vassal of <b>Yelü Dashi</b>'s Qara Khitai in 1134 and in 1209 its ruler, the Idiqut Barchuk Art Tegin, submitted to Genghis Khan, after which Uyghurs served as civil servants of the Mongol Empire, which adopted the Old Uyghur alphabet as its official script.</blockquote><a href="/empire/uyghur-khaganate">Uyghur Khaganate · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>On the Qatwan steppe north of Samarkand, the Qara Khitai under <b>Yelü Dashi</b> encircled and destroyed the army of the Seljuk sultan Ahmad Sanjar, who barely escaped.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-9">9 September in history</a></li><li><blockquote>With commanders such as <b>Yelü Dashi</b>, its army defeated two Song Dynasty attempts to take Yanjing in 1122, revealing Song weakness to the Jurchen.</blockquote><a href="/state/northern-liao">Northern Liao</a></li></ul></section>
